# 26.11.1

## New Features

 . HTTP QUERY method (RFC 10008); form bodies are parsed into $request->post like POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE (#414)
 . CURLOPT_PROTOCOLS_STR and CURLOPT_REDIR_PROTOCOLS_STR in the native curl hook; with open_basedir set, values with "file" or "all" are refused (#412)
 . Bundled llhttp upgraded to 9.4.4 (#413)

## Changes

 . The HTTP parser is stricter: a space before a header colon, folded header lines and raw bytes above 0x7F in the request target get 400 Bad Request, in the server and the Coroutine HTTP client
 . The WebSocket server follows RFC 6455: unmasked client frames, unknown opcodes and a new message sent before a fragmented one is finished close the connection; ping, pong and close frames accept payloads up to 125 bytes
 . The HTTP/2 server rejects frames on a stream the client has closed, removes the padding of DATA frames, checks WINDOW_UPDATE increments, and with send_yield waits for the stream window
 . SOCKS5 proxy target hosts, usernames and passwords longer than 255 bytes are refused, and a refused CONNECT reply fails the connection

## Bug Fixes

 . Fix WebSocket frames losing their opcode and FIN flag with several reactor threads in SWOOLE_PROCESS mode
 . Fix WebSocket connections when the upgrade request is followed by more data in the same packet
 . Fix a fragmented WebSocket message with an empty first frame losing its opcode
 . Fix the payload of WebSocket ping and pong frames sent with the 16 bit length form
 . Fix multipart form data of an unfinished part being kept for the next request, and its temporary file and memory not being released
 . Fix Request::create()->parse() with a multipart body
 . Fix Response::create() with a Coroutine\Socket
 . Fix chunked requests with Content-Length: 0 that do not end with a zero length chunk
 . Fix client certificates larger than the read buffer with ssl_client_cert_file
 . Fix DTLS connections above max_connection
 . Fix HTTP/2 GOAWAY frames carrying the error code in the flags
 . Fix buffer_high_watermark and buffer_low_watermark being reset when the server starts
 . Fix the $row argument of the PostgreSQL statement fetch methods being ignored
 . Fix a Lock becoming unusable in other processes after a child process exits
 . Fix a Table losing rows with concurrent writers after a child process exits
 . Fix Lock::lockwait() requiring an argument
 . Fix the open_redis_protocol parser with null bulk strings, integer elements and empty arrays
 . Fix the length protocol with unsigned 32 bit lengths of 2^31 and more
 . Fix the SOCKS5 handshake with short replies and IPv4 targets
 . Fix Coroutine\Client::peek() with a length of 0 or less
 . Fix curl_setopt_array() not stopping at a refused option in the native curl hook

# 26.11.0

## New Features

 . PHP 8.6 support
 . CURLOPT_SEEKFUNCTION support in the native curl hook on PHP 8.6
 . CURLOPT_PREREQFUNCTION support in the native curl hook on PHP 8.4+ (Guzzle 7.12+)
 . PIE (PHP Installer for Extensions) support
 . Response::cookie() also sends Max-Age when an expiry time is set, like setcookie() (#310)

## Changes

 . Hooked ssl:// and tls:// client streams use the same peer verification defaults as native PHP; set verify_peer to false to connect to servers with a self-signed certificate
 . Cookie values are encoded and decoded like PHP does: a "+" is kept and a space is %20, in the server and the HTTP clients; cookies with spaces set by earlier versions read back with "+" until they are set again; for a cookie name sent twice, the first value is used (#311)
 . OpenSwoole 27.2 will require PHP 8.4 or later; 26.11 is the last release series to support PHP 8.3

## Bug Fixes

 . Fix stream_socket_enable_crypto with tls (#401)
 . Fix io_uring build on Alpine Linux (#400)
 . Fix SSL client certificate lost in getClientInfo() when the worker pid is greater than 65535
 . Fix curl_copy_handle() not keeping the CURLOPT_STDERR stream and callback data in the native curl hook
 . Fix preemptive scheduler crash on ZTS builds
 . Fix crash in the native curl hook when a curl multi handle is released after the event loop is destroyed
 . Fix enable_reuse_port having no effect on Linux because SO_REUSEPORT was not detected at configure time
 . Fix the http2_* server settings being ignored and not sent to clients in the SETTINGS frame
 . Fix max_idle_time closing active connections and ignoring fractions of a second
 . Fix a crash when a coroutine is canceled during file I/O
 . Fix stream_select() closing regular files
 . Fix closing a unix datagram socket removing the peer's socket file
 . Fix process pipes never being closed
 . Fix Lock::lockwait() truncating the timeout
 . Fix process pool reload stalling, getProcess() ids and a connection leak
 . Fix process pool warnings about workers that already exited or detached
 . Fix the signal listener count with wait_signal
 . Fix a second Coroutine\System::waitSignal() on the same signal leaving the first waiting forever
 . Fix Coroutine::select() with push channels and array keys
 . Fix Table keys longer than 63 bytes, iteration with an empty key, and incr()/decr() on a bad column
 . Fix the Table row lock being taken over from a live holder
 . Fix an HTTP/2 RST_STREAM leaving a send_yield coroutine waiting forever
 . Fix the open_redis_protocol parser failing on commands split across reads and on pipelined commands
 . Fix hooked time_nanosleep() accepting nanoseconds out of range
 . Fix a crash in the native curl hook with curl_copy_handle() or connection reuse in curl_multi
 . Fix curl_reset() losing the coroutine state of a native curl handle
 . Fix co::run() not returning for minutes after curl_multi requests in the native curl hook
 . Fix io_uring warnings logged on every file operation when io_uring is not available, for example in Docker containers with the default seccomp profile
 . Fix the server master process being killed by SIGALRM when a timer was created before Server::start()
 . Fix the static handler sending the file body for HEAD requests
 . Fix the HTTP/2 client reply to PING frames and its handling of GOAWAY and padded frames
 . Fix CurlHandle objects never being freed with CURLOPT_HEADERFUNCTION in the native curl hook on PHP 8.4+ (#391)
 . Fix HTTP/2 server responses to HEAD requests sending a body
 . Fix bundled hiredis symbols colliding with other extensions that link hiredis (#394)
 . Fix the build on FreeBSD 14 and 15 (#389)
 . Fix OpenSwoole\Table ignoring a conflictProportion below 1 (#362)
 . Fix the io_uring reactor failing to start when io_uring is not available; it now falls back to epoll, and reactor_type is accepted by Server::set() (#408)
 . Fix HTTP/2 requests with headers split into CONTINUATION frames, and HPACK errors when http2_header_table_size is set (#388)
 . Fix heap corruption when closing a mysqli connection opened with mysqli_init() and real_connect() in a coroutine (#409, #378)
 . Fix max_request_execution_time ending later requests early and crashing workers (#315, #358)
 . Fix coroutines crashing when opcache.preload is enabled (#343)
 . Fix the deprecation warning for on('handshake') (#303)
 . Fix configure not finding libpq in lib64 without pg_config (#245)
 . Fix task workers logging a warning for SIGPIPE
 . Fix Xdebug not seeing the request callback with use_fiber_context, which crashed the worker when variables were inspected (#404)
 . Fix the io_uring reactor not answering requests in SWOOLE_PROCESS mode (#405)
 . Fix the io_uring reactor on kernels before 5.13, where multishot poll is not available
 . Various stability fixes

# 26.2.0

## New Features

 . PHP 8.5 support
 . PHP native Fiber context backend for coroutines: new coroutine context backend using PHP's native zend_fiber API instead of Boost ASM or ucontext. Enables proper integration with xdebug, profilers, and fiber-aware extensions. Configurable at runtime via `Co::set(['use_fiber_context' => true])` or INI `openswoole.use_fiber_context=On`
 . Xdebug support: xdebug step debugging now works correctly inside coroutines when fiber context is enabled. Removed the legacy "extremely dangerous" warning
 . Runtime reactor type selection: select the event reactor backend at runtime via `Co::set(['reactor_type' => OPENSWOOLE_IO_URING])`. New constants: OPENSWOOLE_EPOLL, OPENSWOOLE_KQUEUE, OPENSWOOLE_POLL, OPENSWOOLE_SELECT, OPENSWOOLE_IO_URING
 . io_uring reactor backend: new event reactor using Linux io_uring with IORING_OP_POLL_ADD as a drop-in replacement for epoll. Enable with `--enable-io-uring` (requires liburing). Supports multishot poll on kernel 5.13+ with automatic fallback on older kernels
 . io_uring async file I/O engine: dedicated io_uring ring for asynchronous file operations (open, read, write, fstat, fsync, unlink, rename, mkdir, rmdir), replacing the thread pool. Unsupported operations gracefully fall back to the thread pool
 . Event loop lag metrics: real-time event loop lag monitoring via `$server->stats()`. Exposes `event_loop_lag_ms`, `event_loop_lag_max_ms`, and `event_loop_lag_avg_ms` per worker, task worker (when coroutine-enabled), and reactor thread (process mode). Useful for detecting blocking operations that stall the event loop
 . Coroutine-safe exit() support: intercepts exit() calls inside coroutines on PHP 8.4+ (where exit changed from opcode to function) and throws openswoole_exit_exception instead
 . Backward compatibility constant aliases
 . Migrate HTTP parser to llhttp: replaces the custom openswoole_http_parser with llhttp parser for improved standards compliance and performance

## Bug Fixes

 . Fix reflection issues and scope leaks (#284): OSW_FUNCTION_ALIAS caused global functions to appear as class methods with corrupted return types in Reflection. Replaced with proper PHP_FE/PHP_FALIAS entries
 . Fix file I/O hanging under io_uring: race condition where eventfd notification could be lost between draining and re-arming single-shot POLL_ADD. Added reactor end-of-loop callback and timeout CQE filtering
 . Fix file lock bug: non-blocking flock (LOCK_NB) now properly checks in-process coroutine lock state before the system flock() call
 . Fix CPU affinity compile check: add missing _GNU_SOURCE define before sched.h
 . Fix futex compile check: add missing _GNU_SOURCE define before linux/futex.h

## Refactoring

 . Namespace normalization: openswoole_*, updated internal references and test directories
 . Removed compile-time guards from reactor type PHP constants; runtime validation handles unsupported backends
 . Removed PHP < 8.0 compatibility code
 . Dropped PHP 8.2 support

